","t":"Hmm.... senior traders should answer this. I just think no. 2 is DP (origin/dp to engulf), which might/might not be followed by 1 (which is the important FL). I think the ideal use of trade would be: If FL2 is origin/DP to/for FL1, then an engulf of FL1 that hasnot reached FL2 is tradeable, hence DP/Origin of engulf of FL1 would be an ideal entry for FL2 as target.\n\nHopefully a senior can correct me if i'm wrong.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1041","p":42,"im":[],"m":1041},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1042","t":"Jurij\n\nI see that the DP concept causes so much confusion. Sometimes price respects the DP sometimes not. Then the always recurring question, does an eng have to eng the DP too?\n\nBut think about DP, what is really a DP? This is my view on it:\n\nThis is what we see\n\nfrequency\n\n1356\n\nThis is in terms of orders\n\nThere's no DP, only order flow and new transactions (FL). Again just my understanding","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1042","p":42,"im":["17c8642506a17f04ab745ae84441786b162d67f0","bbeb2143724e61e2aac05910ce4d7d9c45d7a2bf"],"m":1042},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1043","t":"Jurij that's interesting. But what about these 2 cases I've found in Gold. If my FL are drawn correctly, looks like price FO beyond the FL, just to where it was the DP to engulf previous FL....any idea?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1043","p":42,"im":["accd44ac8973b4b9cd28125f235937334a28b4dc"],"m":1043},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1044","t":"Hi franc464, thank you for sharing that chart. it s a truly an eye opener. everything from FL, engulf, DP - thank you for sharing (and teaching) me indirectly.\n\nI've seen similar structure, but i'm sure it's different. could you please note the difference from this chart? Maybe compare between the two. so we all can learn? Yours could be much tidier than mine.:P\n\n2144","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1044","p":42,"im":["115c3949a69288aadfe9703a5021dff1119b168a"],"m":1044},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1045","t":"Sorry Staurum, don't understand your question and don't see any level drawn on your chart","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1045","p":42,"im":[],"m":1045},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1046","t":"staurum wrote: Hmm.... senior traders should answer this. I just think no. 2 is DP (origin/dp to engulf), which might/might not be followed by 1 (which is the important FL). I think the ideal use of trade would be: If FL2 is origin/DP to/for FL1, then an engulf of FL1 that hasnot reached FL2 is tradeable, hence DP/Origin of engulf of FL1 would be an ideal entry for FL2 as target.\n\nHopefully a senior can correct me if i'm wrong.\n\nHello dear friend.. Thanks for the comments that you made. I think you mean image below has been named the No. 2 which I think is a FTR. AND NOT BE AN FL..","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1046","p":42,"im":["d743f115637133e81672fb1351d4a8708ccb0697"],"m":1046},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1047","t":"Jurij\n\nfranc464 wrote: Jurij that's interesting. But what about these 2 cases I've found in Gold. If my FL are drawn correctly, looks like price FO beyond the FL, just to where it was the DP to engulf previous FL....any idea?\n\nfrequency\n\n1356\n\nHi franc, yes price can FO to a DP. I'm just saying a there's no DP, just lower scale FLs. When price decides to fake out to some place it is usually a FL, in case of DP, a lower scale FL.\n\nAbout the lower level, I haven't found an answer to why price jumped there, this could look like a real DP, but keep in mind there's also a CPAZ below, so maybe it is reacting to the demand before the PAZ. Perhaps it was just a demand and price is not done yet with lower prices until it hits a proper target. This is my understanding, because this way there's no need for DPs in my analysis, only FLs. As we know, price travels from FL to FL.\n\nGood question and interesting discussion","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1047","p":42,"im":["accd44ac8973b4b9cd28125f235937334a28b4dc","e748d52b2d48afb8a5071fedf7b1a9279c73e78b","927bf03d4b8f5cdc72558c9fbae496bb29a56211"],"m":1047},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1048","t":"Hi Jurij and any senior, please cmiiw,\n\n2144\n\nThe drop from 1190 to 1170, I've marked 4 supply zones. My basic thought was, when rallying price engulfs each zone (start from lower to the top), it might target the next upper supply zone.\n\nBefore the each engulf is origin, after engulf if price does not return to origin, it might create FTR or FL. If it returns to origin and break north, Price just made a FL sitting on top of its origin. Each created FTR/FL could be target for bounce should price falls to it.\n\nIF said that every engulf has a target. Salivan wrote a theory about electromagnetic-repulsion for the moves after engulf. I still have not studied it full, but i think Salivan's theory must be reliable here.\n\nCheers,","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1048","p":42,"im":["22155cc9dbd94e3ff905fb3baf7b563026b1d48c"],"m":1048},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1049","t":"incoming.....................\n\n2144","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1049","p":42,"im":["9352944a970aaccdc4d650b4a2fea24410b6f124","21379ef6e3a9ffa4cf5ce9108eb831dab1710827","d19085cf09ae03572378ccf345d00aa0b0ac4490","fd9daa4fb94bb975c5decd50718d04d970603b8f","0ba7641116c8ee47831d3c1cb255f4c85523ee0b","c4f335465b360e38ca27903cbf094eb34c645513","26c46d39382a764f669521c91fcaa550150b9efe","2d55ba22676e585ff411f6e5447843784daaf7f4","e540b955ddfdb91bcc6cd59ce3ed541ccc9ee4ea","5199bd20c6e7a0e3ad9def9d82450dac274d25a1"],"m":1049},{"id":"flaglimits_p42_1050","t":"Hello, guys)\n\nSome charts from Russian futures markets in Fl HW from me. Is it correct? Not for sure about one (SBERBANK pic №2), when price breakes local HI and while return creates (?) the FL.\n\nThanks for comments and sorry for my English anyway)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1050","p":42,"im":["1486d6574b46a38b559adf71df5d634d3cec9f6a","ec54a1794a8d4eebcbc5a680a4faf456ebf9946f","ba1af0f7587cbc2a6589e1a40f68f5cf3b3c4c4c","fecc77219f156d00f501eaa4b2547a75da71f17a"],"m":1050}],"images":[{"k":"705f839eec0ae276e68da6f8ac2fff50724a0415","t":"assets/thumbs/705f839eec0ae276e68da6f8ac2fff50724a0415.webp","f":"